mWizard
=======

mWizard is a lightweight window manager for the X Window System, built on the
Motif toolkit.

It is a fork of EMWM (https://github.com/alx210/emwm), which derives from The
Open Group's Motif Window Manager. mWizard removes the parts of EMWM that
depended on, or interfered with, other software, and consolidates configuration
into a single rc file.

Notably, mWizard does not draw a backdrop over the root window, so root-window
wallpaper setters such as feh(1), xsetroot(1), hsetroot(1) and xwallpaper(1)
work as expected. See NOTICE for the full list of changes and for licensing
information.

mWizard is distributed under the GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1
or later; see COPYING.


PREREQUISITES
=============

C99 compliant C compiler
POSIX compliant make

Libraries and Headers required for building:

libX11
libXt
libXext
libXrandr
libXinerama
libXm (open-motif/motif)

Optional, only when the idle-lock timer is enabled (-DIDLE_LOCK, on by
default in src/common.mf):

libXScrnSaver (libXss)

To build without it, remove -DIDLE_LOCK from DEFINES and -lXss from SYSLIBS in
src/common.mf. Everything else in mWizard builds with no additional
dependencies beyond those EMWM already required.

BUILDING AND INSTALLING
=======================

Make sure to review the target platform makefile (mf/Makefile.<platform>).
Adjust the installation prefix and X resources installation path if necessary.
Read comments in the makefile for additional compile time options available.
The target platform is picked by the master Makefile from uname(1). If no
platform specific Makefile exists, try "Makefile.generic".

Run 'make' in the top-level directory of the source distribution.
When the build process finishes, run 'make install' as root.

CONFIGURATION
=======================

mWizard is configured from a single rc file. A sample is installed as
PREFIX/X11/system.mwizardrc; copy it to $HOME/.mwizardrc to customize. It
defines key and mouse bindings, menus, and, in its Settings and Client blocks,
window manager behaviour.

doc/CONFIGURATION.md is the full guide to that file, including a table
mapping every former X resource to its new rc setting.

The app-defaults file installed in PREFIX/X11/app-defaults/MWizard now carries
appearance settings only: colors, shadows and fonts. Behaviour settings that
EMWM read from the X resource database are read from the rc file instead, and
the rc file takes precedence over any leftover entries in .Xdefaults.

The mwizardrc(4) man page describes the file syntax in detail, and mwizard(1)
documents the remaining appearance resources.

MIGRATING FROM EMWM
=======================

An existing ~/.emwmrc will not be read; copy it to ~/.mwizardrc. Bindings and
menus carry over unchanged, except that f.set_behavior no longer exists.

Behaviour settings in ~/.Xdefaults or an old Emwm app-defaults file are no
longer consulted; move them into a Settings block in ~/.mwizardrc. Backdrop
resources have no replacement -- use a root-window wallpaper setter instead.

See the "Migrating from EMWM" section of doc/CONFIGURATION.md for the details.
